<title>HONG KONG: China World Trade Center may seek H-share listing.</title>
<headline>China World Trade Center may seek H-share listing.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shangri-La Asia Ltd unit China World Trade Center Ltd may seek an H-share listing, Shangri-La Asia managing director Paul Bush said on Friday.</p>
<p>China World Trade Center (CWTC) is 50 percent owned by Shangri-La Asia.</p>
<p>&quot;There are indications that it (CWTC) may be an H-share listing,&quot; Bush told reporters after Shangri-La Asia's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>The China Securities and Regulatory Commission earlier this year approved CWTC's request to seek an overseas listing.</p>
<p>H-shares are shares of China-incorporated companies listed on the Hong Kong stock market.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371  http://www.hk97.com</p>
